# Story 4: Configuring Rysh (45s)
# Hook: One config file. Environment overrides. Full control.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-04-configuring-rysh.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:02.0]
One config file. Environment overrides. Full control.

[00:02.0 --> 00:08.0]
Rysh looks for its config at ~/.config/rysh/rysh.config. It uses TOML format -- clean and readable.

[00:08.0 --> 00:15.0]
The provider section sets your AI backend and API key.

[00:15.0 --> 00:22.0]
The ui section controls how rysh looks and behaves on launch.

[00:22.0 --> 00:29.0]
The upstream section enables remote features and collaboration.

[00:29.0 --> 00:37.0]
Every config option can be overridden with an environment variable. Prefix with RYSH_ and you're set.

[00:37.0 --> 00:42.0]
That's all you need. Config file for defaults, env vars for overrides.

